# Command Index ([PROJECT_NAME])

Read when: a routine repo command is needed quickly and the current task doc does not already name it.
Skip when: the active artifact already gives the exact command to run.

Purpose: give AI agents and operators one thin, authoritative place for the commands used repeatedly in normal work so future sessions do not have to rediscover them from multiple docs.

This file is the quick index.
Keep it updated when verify, test, run, package, deploy, or maintenance commands change.

## Core Commands

| Goal | Command | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Canonical verify gate | `[VERIFY_COMMAND]` | Required before handoff |
| Regenerate AI/system context | `[AI_CONTEXT_COMMAND]` | If this project uses `AI_CONTEXT.md` |
| Template drift check | `bash scripts/check_template_drift.sh . /path/to/templates-v2` | Update the source-pack path for this repo |
| Template validation | `bash scripts/validate_templates.sh .` | If this project ships the validator |
| Same-change doc enforcement | `bash scripts/enforce_doc_updates.sh` | If this project ships the guardrail |
| Predeploy/release gate | `bash scripts/predeploy_full_suite.sh` | Use `N/A` if the repo has no predeploy gate |

